# cedian_worktree_request — cedian_worktree_request

cedian's own host tool (trusted). Ask the cedian IDE for an isolated git worktree for a parallel worker, with its brief (goal, scope.write, acceptance, verify, timebox_min); never run `git worktree add` yourself. Returns the worktree id and path.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** worker id: [A-Za-z0-9._-] */
  id: string;
  /** one sentence: what the worker is for */
  goal: string;
  scope: {
    /** path globs the worker may write */
    write: string[];
    /** path globs it must not write */
    deny?: string[];
  };
  /** checkable lines that say it is done */
  acceptance: string[];
  /** commands or verification-profile ids that check it */
  verify: string[];
  /** minutes before it shows as stuck */
  timebox_min: number;
  /** file and PR pointers */
  context?: string[];
  /** what it must not do */
  forbidden?: string[];
  kind?: string;
  /** branch or commit (default HEAD) */
  base?: string;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://cedian_worktree_request.

